        "id": 18826,
        "name": "SwiftBot",
        "username": "SwiftBot",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/f6c823/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-12-26T15:39:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>(mild spoilers)</p>\n<p>I have a very simple question about all mission/reward cards, that doesn't seem to be addressed in the rulebook.</p>\n<p>When a mission card flips, is the reward put in my hand? Is it put in my play area?</p>\n<p>Is the answer different depending on what type it is?</p>\n<p>So far, an internet search has turned up a few posts that hint at rewards going to hand except for targets, and a&nbsp;Kickstarter page from before release&nbsp;that suggests one-shots should go in my hand but all others directly into play. So I'm seeing many different possibilities, and nothing to clarify what rule was actually intended by the designers.</p>\n<p>Can someone clarify this for me?</p>\n<p>I have to say, I love Sentinels and I'm really looking forward to trying Oblivaeon... I'm just disappointed that such a basic game rule is not covered in the rulebook! I imagine it seems obvious to some, but it is not obvious to me. When a card has so many different states it could be in, it really helps to have a clear explanation of how those states change.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:18.987Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 2,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 10.0,
